          "text": "$-\\dfrac{11}{(2x + 1)^{2}}$",
          "why": "Swapped the numerator terms to compute $uv' - u'v$."
        },
        {
          "text": "$\\dfrac{20x - 1}{(2x + 1)^{2}}$",
          "why": "Added the numerator terms instead of subtracting."
        },
        {
          "text": "$\\dfrac{5}{2}$",
          "why": "Differentiated numerator and denominator separately."
        }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$u = 5x - 3, \\quad u' = 5$\n$v = 2x + 1, \\quad v' = 2$\n$y' = \\dfrac{5(2x + 1) - 2(5x - 3)}{(2x + 1)^{2}}$\n$= \\dfrac{10x + 5 - 10x + 6}{(2x + 1)^{2}}$\n$= \\dfrac{11}{(2x + 1)^{2}}$"
